    \item \textbf{Negative results define method boundaries.} No alternative method consistently matches supervised probing across all four models (\cref{tab:negative}): BOCPD/CUSUM fail on gradual transitions; Mahalanobis distance finds near-zero separation; RepE achieves competitive balanced accuracy on QwQ-32B (0.756 vs.\ supervised 0.778) but at substantially lower precision (0.512 vs.\ 0.700), illustrating metric-dependent comparison; cross-model transfer fails under PCA alignment. Control task selectivity (12.5--19.7pp above chance; \cref{app:control}) confirms genuine safety structure.
\end{itemize}

\noindent Our results characterize the safety commitment phenomenon rather than constitute production detectors: false positive rates remain 39--52\%, and the 85.5\% oracle gap (\cref{sec:discussion}) underscores how much room remains for improvement.

